<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">O'Malley clan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ó Máille</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The O'Malleys (Ó Máille) were a Gaelic seafaring lineage of Umall, around Clew Bay in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-mayo">County Mayo</a>, western Ireland. Unusual among Irish lords for their fleets, they fished, traded and raided along the Atlantic coast and paid dues to the Mac William <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-burgh">Burkes</a>. The best-known member was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grace-omalley">Grace O'Malley</a>, the 16th-century sea captain who met <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> in 1593.</p></div>
